The attached image illustrates the in vivo kinetics and cellular targeting of Nano-11 nanoparticles in the draining lymph node. Flow cytometry plots and corresponding bar graphs demonstrate that Nano-11-containing myeloid cells appear in the lymph node, peaking at Day 2, with the majority (60-80%) identified as migratory dendritic cells (MigDC). MigDCs also exhibit the highest mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) for Nano-11, indicating these cells internalize more nanoparticles per cell compared to lymphoid tissue resident DCs (LTDCs) and monocytes/macrophages (Mo/MΦ), confirming Nano-11's effective and preferential delivery to MigDCs.